"""Single-point mutants of experiments/exp_speed2.py, for tools/mutants.py:

    venv/bin/python tools/mutants.py --exp exp_speed2 --tests tests/test_exp_speed2.py --raw results/smlm/speed2_raw.npz --md results/smlm/speed2.md \\
        --extra results/smlm/speed2.md --out-env SPEED2_OUT --spec tools/mutants/wp_speed2_own.py --work <scratch dir>

A tuple is (id, what, old, new[, k]): `old` replaced by `new` at its k-th occurrence (0-based) in experiments/exp_speed2.py. The kill criterion is the tests file alone; it includes the byte-for-byte
regeneration of the stored report from the stored raw. The run parts (E, V, T, P, S, A, AF) need the data and are not exercised by the tests, so their mutants are not in this list.

Result (tests/test_exp_speed2.py, 31 tests, 78 mutants; OMP_NUM_THREADS=1): all 78 are killed. (Wording round after the referee report A+B: W01-W26 added, 39 tests: W01, the pooled mean of the sets' means divided by one instead of the number of sets, is EQUIVALENT, since every pooled ratio is a ratio of two such means and the factor cancels; the other 25 are killed, after tests were added for W14, W16, W21, W24, W25. The slot needs `--extra results/smlm/speed2_plan.md` as well.) A first run left 7 alive (pairing by one column, the barred set compared in length only, the width and the
four astronomy criteria alone in the verdict); the tests `compare_dets_pairs_detections_that_share_a_column`, the barred-set case and `each_single_criterion_alone_fails_the_verdict` killed them.
"""
